  "worked_solution": "From part 1, we have $q=\u27e80,-3,2\u27e9$ and $r=\u27e80,4,3\u27e9.$\n\nAlso, from part 2, we have $x=r-q$\n\nTo compute the difference of two vectors, we just subtract each component individually:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r-q & =\u27e80,4,3\u27e9-\u27e80,-3,2\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e80-0,4-(-3),3-2\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e80,7,1\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $x=\u27e80,7,1\u27e9.$",
